---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const portfolio = [
  { img: 'pump-nozzle', caption: '3D-printed nozzle adapter for a mattress air pump' },
  { img: 'fridge-handle-mount', caption: 'Replacement refrigerator handle mount' },
  { img: 'beach-jamz-lithophane', caption: 'Lithophane of a Beach Jamz session — light reveals the photo' },
  { img: 'soap-dish', caption: 'Draining soap dish' },
  { img: 'extruder-lever', caption: 'Printed extruder lever — the printer repairing itself' },
  { img: 'logo-plaque', caption: 'Two-color logo plaque for a local business' },
  { img: 'throwing-knife', caption: 'Practice throwing knife (plastic)' },
  { img: 'mask-print', caption: 'Mask components mid-print' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Past Work — Peace Antz"
  description="The honest history of Peace Antz: blockchain validators, an on-demand 3D printing workshop, beach jams, and the original DAO — what we built and what we learned."
>
  <section class="section--tight" style="padding-top: 2.5rem">
    <div class="container center">
      <span class="kicker">Our history</span>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.9rem)">Past Work</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-inline: auto">
        Completed chapters, told truthfully. None of these are active services
        today — some may return; see the <a href="/vision">roadmap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container prose reveal">
      <h2><span class="pill pill--past" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 0.6rem">First chapter</span> The band</h2>
      <p>
        Peace Antz started as a band. The most beloved expression of it was
        <strong>Beach Jamz</strong> — live sessions by the water, drums and
        amps in the sand. Music is where the name, the spirit, and the
        friendships came from, and everything that followed grew out of it.
        One relic bridges two eras below: a 3D-printed lithophane that reveals
        a photograph of a Beach Jamz session when you hold it up to the light.
        Music isn’t gone from the vision — it’s resting, like the printer,
        and it has a place on the <a href="/vision">roadmap</a>.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="pill pill--past" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 0.6rem">Workshop era</span> The 3D printing workshop</h2>
      <p>
        “Antz Designz” was an on-demand printing service: send an STL file,
        get a part. Most of the joy was in repair — printing the little
        irreplaceable pieces that keep household things out of the landfill: a
        pump nozzle, a fridge handle mount, drawer guides, a door latch. It
        also made art: lithophanes that reveal a photograph when held to the
        light. The printer is currently idle; the portfolio below is the real
        record.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="container reveal" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
      <div class="gallery">
        {portfolio.map((p) => (
          <figure>
            <img src={`/images/past-work/${p.img}.jpg`} alt={p.caption} loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>{p.caption}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container prose reveal">
      <h2><span class="pill pill--past" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 0.6rem">Validator era</span> Running real infrastructure</h2>
      <p>
        Peace Antz ran real blockchain infrastructure. A validator on the
        Findora network proposed over 1,600 blocks with 96% uptime before that
        network itself wound down. More meaningfully, we operated the
        <strong>Recovery Validator</strong> on Harmony — a community-DAO node
        (originally created by Matthew Barrett) that directed rewards toward
        helping people recover from the Horizon bridge incident, sustained by
        56 delegators at 99.6% uptime. Running dependable infrastructure for a
        community-repair effort remains one of the clearest expressions of what
        Peace Antz values. Both validators are now retired.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="pill pill--past" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 0.6rem">DAO chapter</span> The constitution</h2>
      <p>
        The original Peace Antz DAO had a full written constitution: an ANTZ
        reputation token, ant-colony roles from Worker to Queen, elections
        timed to Bitcoin halvings, and a consultation-flavored justice system.
        The community it imagined never fully materialized, but the document
        captures real thought about fair governance, and pieces of it will
        inform whatever community structure comes next. It is preserved
        verbatim in the <a href="/archive/constitution-v1">archive</a>.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="pill pill--past" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 0.6rem">The bridge</span> The BahAI Workforce</h2>
      <p>
        Our bridge between chapters: a local-first team of AI agents that
        designs Bahá’í-inspired bookmarks and giveaway quote cards under
        code-enforced honesty rules — quotes verified against the writings and
        locked, AI artwork always disclosed, marketing claims scrubbed by code
        rather than by promise. It has produced dozens of print-ready cards,
        and it is the direct ancestor of this site’s
        <a href="/create">Quote Card Creator</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="gallery" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(160px, 1fr)); margin-top: 1.4rem">
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/cards/card-war-to-peace.jpg" alt="Workforce quote card in English" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Giveaway card, English</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/cards/card-war-to-peace-zh.jpg" alt="The same quote card, AI-assisted Chinese translation with printed disclaimer" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Same card — labeled AI-assisted translation</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/cards/bookmark-tabernacle.jpg" alt="Print-ready bookmark with AI artwork" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Print-ready bookmark face</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/images/cards/bookmark-2.jpg" alt="A second print-ready bookmark design" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Bookmark design</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container center reveal">
      <p class="lead" style="margin-inline: auto">
        Drone flights, podcasts-in-waiting, and other smaller stories live in
        the same era. If one matters to you, <a href="/contact">ask us about it</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
